   "html": "<h2 id=\"what-you-get\">What you get <a class=\"docs-anchor\" href=\"#what-you-get\" aria-label=\"Link to What you get\">#</a></h2>\n<p>At the end of these five steps, an agent on your computer shows its work live on your iPhone's Lock\nScreen, asks before risky steps, and tells you once when it is done. Every script and app you connect\nlater uses the same server and the same phone.</p>\n<aside class=\"docs-callout\" data-tone=\"tip\"><p class=\"docs-callout-title\">Server and phone already done?</p>\n<p>Paste one line into your coding agent and it connects this computer for you: the CLI, the sign-in, and\nevery agent's skill and instructions. See <a href=\"/docs/get-started/with-an-agent\">Set up with your agent</a>.</p>\n</aside>\n<h2 id=\"what-you-need\">What you need <a class=\"docs-anchor\" href=\"#what-you-need\" aria-label=\"Link to What you need\">#</a></h2>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>A server host:</strong> Linux or macOS with Git, OpenSSL, Docker and Docker Compose v2. It can be the\ncomputer you work on, a home server or a cloud machine.</li>\n<li><strong>An address for it</strong> that your iPhone and every computer can reach, over HTTPS. For a trial on one\ncomputer, <code>http://localhost:8180</code> is enough.</li>\n<li><strong>A Mac with Xcode,</strong> a physical iPhone with Developer Mode on, and an Apple Developer Program\nmembership to build and sign the app.</li>\n<li><strong>An Apple push key</strong> (<code>.p8</code>), with its Key ID and your Team ID, so the server can reach the phone.</li>\n<li><strong>Node.js 22 or newer</strong> on each computer that runs the <code>relo</code> CLI.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>You can run the server and the Dashboard without the Apple steps, but nothing reaches the phone until\nthey are done.</p>\n<h2 id=\"the-five-steps\">The five steps <a class=\"docs-anchor\" href=\"#the-five-steps\" aria-label=\"Link to The five steps\">#</a></h2>\n<ul class=\"docs-tiles\">\n<li><a href=\"/docs/get-started/server\"><strong>1. Run the server</strong>Docker Compose, your address, secrets and the owner account. About 15 minutes.</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/docs/get-started/iphone\"><strong>2. Install the iPhone app</strong>Build and sign in Xcode, create your account, allow notifications, turn on push. About 20 minutes.</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/docs/get-started/cli\"><strong>3. Connect this computer</strong>Connect a computer with one command or one agent prompt, check with relo doctor. About 5 minutes.</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/docs/get-started/first-card\"><strong>4. See your first card</strong>A test card, then a real work with a plan, a question and an outcome. About 5 minutes.</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/docs/get-started/agents\"><strong>5. Tell your agents</strong>One command for every agent on this computer, then one sentence. About 5 minutes.</a></li>\n</ul>\n<p>Each step ends with a check you can run. If one fails, <a href=\"/docs/troubleshooting\">Troubleshooting</a> starts\nfrom its exact output.</p>\n<h2 id=\"only-connecting-another-computer\">Only connecting another computer? <a class=\"docs-anchor\" href=\"#only-connecting-another-computer\" aria-label=\"Link to Only connecting another computer?\">#</a></h2>\n<p>The server and the phone are done once. For each further computer, <strong>Connect a computer</strong> (iPhone: Settings →\nDevices → Add a computer; Dashboard: Account → Computers → Add a computer; or <code>relo auth invite</code> on a signed-in\ncomputer) gives one command that installs, signs in and sets up, or a prompt for your agent:</p>\n<figure class=\"docs-code\" data-language=\"sh\"><button class=\"docs-copy\" type=\"button\" data-copy=\"curl -fsSL https://relo.example.com/install.sh | sh -s -- rci_…\" hidden>Copy</button><pre><code>curl -fsSL https://relo.example.com/install.sh | sh -s -- rci_…</code></pre></figure>\n",
