   "summary": "The relo CLI on this computer, signed in to your server, so its agents and scripts can report to your phone.",
   "section": "Get started",
   "group": null,
   "html": "<h2 id=\"what-you-get\">What you get <a class=\"docs-anchor\" href=\"#what-you-get\" aria-label=\"Link to What you get\">#</a></h2>\n<p>The <code>relo</code> CLI is how every agent and script on a computer talks to Relo. It keeps each session's\nwork, encrypts it for your phones and sends only the changes. Install it once per computer; each\ncomputer gets its own credential that you can revoke on its own.</p>\n<h2 id=\"the-fastest-way-one-command\">The fastest way: one command <a class=\"docs-anchor\" href=\"#the-fastest-way-one-command\" aria-label=\"Link to The fastest way: one command\">#</a></h2>\n<p>Right after you create your account, <strong>Connect a computer</strong> gives you one command with a one-time code\n(later: Dashboard <strong>Account → Computers → Add a computer</strong>, or iPhone <strong>Settings → Devices → Add a computer</strong>).\nRun it in a terminal on this computer, or on a server over SSH:</p>\n<figure class=\"docs-code\" data-language=\"sh\"><button class=\"docs-copy\" type=\"button\" data-copy=\"curl -fsSL https://relo.example.com/install.sh | sh -s -- rci_…\" hidden>Copy</button><pre><code>curl -fsSL https://relo.example.com/install.sh | sh -s -- rci_…</code></pre></figure>\n<p>It installs the CLI your server hands out (and Node.js 22 if this computer has no recent one), signs this\ncomputer in with no sign-in and sets up the agents you picked. Prefer to let your agent do it? The wizard\nalso gives a prompt for it. See <a href=\"/docs/guides/servers\">Connect a computer</a>.</p>\n<h2 id=\"step-by-step\">Step by step <a class=\"docs-anchor\" href=\"#step-by-step\" aria-label=\"Link to Step by step\">#</a></h2>\n<ol class=\"docs-steps\">\n<li>\n<p><strong>Install the CLI from your server.</strong> It carries the matching agent skill, is checked against its\ndigest, and installs under <code>~/.local/share/relo</code> with a <code>relo</code> launcher in <code>~/.local/bin</code>:</p>\n<figure class=\"docs-code\" data-language=\"sh\"><button class=\"docs-copy\" type=\"button\" data-copy=\"curl -fsSL https://relo.example.com/install.sh | sh\nrelo --version\" hidden>Copy</button><pre><code>curl -fsSL https://relo.example.com/install.sh | sh\nrelo --version</code></pre></figure>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p><strong>Sign in without a code.</strong> Run the login command with your server's address:</p>\n<figure class=\"docs-code\" data-language=\"sh\"><button class=\"docs-copy\" type=\"button\" data-copy=\"relo auth login --api-url &quot;https://relo.example.com&quot;\" hidden>Copy</button><pre><code>relo auth login --api-url &quot;https://relo.example.com&quot;</code></pre></figure>\n<p>The CLI prints a one-time link, a QR code, a code and a two-digit number, and tries to open the link.\nApprove in the Relo app (<strong>Settings → Devices → Sign in a computer</strong>: scan the QR code or type the code) or in the\nbrowser, and pick the number the terminal shows. <code>--no-open</code> keeps the CLI from opening a browser.</p>\n<p>A denied, expired or timed-out request leaves the computer signed out; run the same command again.\nAfter approval, the server address and the credential are kept in a config file only you can read.\nNo command ever takes a token as a flag.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p><strong>Check the computer.</strong></p>\n<figure class=\"docs-code\" data-language=\"sh\"><button class=\"docs-copy\" type=\"button\" data-copy=\"relo auth status\nrelo doctor\" hidden>Copy</button><pre><code>relo auth status\nrelo doctor</code></pre></figure>\n<p><code>relo doctor</code> prints <code>ready</code> and, while something is missing, a <code>next</code> step with the exact command to\nrun: sign in, a phone, then the one-time <code>relo test</code>.</p>\n</li>\n</ol>\n<aside class=\"docs-callout\" data-tone=\"tip\"><p class=\"docs-callout-title\">CI and containers</p>\n<p>A pipeline, or a cloud sandbox such as Claude Code on the web (not a computer), skips the sign-in: set\n<code>RELO_TOKEN</code> and <code>RELO_API_URL</code> from its secret store. See\n<a href=\"/docs/guides/scripts\">Scripts, cron and CI</a>.</p>\n</aside>\n<p>After the computer joins, restart any agent sessions that were already open.</p>\n<h2 id=\"check-it\">Check it <a class=\"docs-anchor\" href=\"#check-it\" aria-label=\"Link to Check it\">#</a></h2>\n<figure class=\"docs-code\" data-language=\"sh\"><button class=\"docs-copy\" type=\"button\" data-copy=\"relo doctor\" hidden>Copy</button><pre><code>relo doctor</code></pre></figure>\n<p>At this point <code>ready</code> is still <code>false</code>, and <code>next.step</code> is <code>test</code>: the server and your phone are known,\nand the last check is a real card on the phone. That is the next step.</p>\n<p>If <code>next.step</code> is <code>login</code>, the sign-in did not complete; if it is <code>phone</code>, open the Relo app, sign in\nand allow Live Activities, then confirm with <code>relo devices list</code>.</p>\n<h2 id=\"several-servers-or-accounts\">Several servers or accounts <a class=\"docs-anchor\" href=\"#several-servers-or-accounts\" aria-label=\"Link to Several servers or accounts\">#</a></h2>\n<p>One computer can hold several sign-ins as profiles (<code>--profile work</code>), switched with\n<code>relo auth switch</code>. See <a href=\"/docs/guides/profiles\">Profiles</a>. To keep the CLI current, see\n<a href=\"/docs/guides/update\">Updating</a>.</p>\n",
