   "markdown": "# Guides\n\nOne task per page: connect your agents, report from scripts and apps, look after this computer and your server.\n\nEach guide does one job. It says why you would want it, then the steps, then how to check it worked.\nFlags live in the [CLI reference](/docs/reference/cli); the guides link to it instead of repeating them.\n\n## Agents\n\nClaude Code, Codex, Gemini CLI, Cursor and other harnesses, on any computer you use.\n\n<ul class=\"docs-tiles\">\n<li><a href=\"/docs/guides/agents\"><strong>Agent harnesses</strong>Tell every agent on this computer about Relo with one command.</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/docs/guides/hooks\"><strong>Depth and hooks</strong>Choose how deep Relo plugs in, and get a live Sessions view.</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/docs/guides/mcp\"><strong>MCP for tools without a shell</strong>Claude desktop, Cursor chat and other clients that cannot run a command.</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/docs/agents\"><strong>For agents</strong>The rules an agent follows, in the words it reads.</a></li>\n</ul>\n\n## Scripts and apps\n\nCron jobs, CI pipelines, deploy tools and your own product.\n\n<ul class=\"docs-tiles\">\n<li><a href=\"/docs/guides/scripts\"><strong>Scripts, cron and CI</strong>Your jobs report progress and outcomes from any script or pipeline.</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/docs/guides/asking\"><strong>Questions from code</strong>Ask before a risky step and act only on an approval.</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/docs/guides/apps\"><strong>Apps and webhooks</strong>Put a person in the loop of your app over HTTP, with signed answers.</a></li>\n</ul>\n\n## This computer\n\n<ul class=\"docs-tiles\">\n<li><a href=\"/docs/guides/profiles\"><strong>Several computers and logins</strong>One login per computer, profiles for separate jobs, names that tell them apart.</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/docs/guides/update\"><strong>Update and uninstall</strong>Move to a verified release, roll back, or remove everything Relo wrote.</a></li>\n</ul>\n\n## Your server\n\n<ul class=\"docs-tiles\">\n<li><a href=\"/docs/guides/origin\"><strong>Your server's address</strong>Put your Relo server behind a public HTTPS origin.</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/docs/guides/accounts\"><strong>Accounts</strong>Who can sign in to your server, and what each account sees.</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/docs/guides/keys\"><strong>Keys and phones</strong>End-to-end encryption keys, new phones and security codes.</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/docs/guides/hardening\"><strong>Hardening</strong>Lock down a server that faces the internet.</a></li>\n</ul>\n",
