   "markdown": "# relo ask, relo interaction and relo listen\n\nEvery command and option that asks you a question and gets your answer back.\n\n`relo ask` puts one question on the open work's card (or, with no card, in a notification with the\nanswer buttons) and waits for your tap. `relo interaction` reads, resumes waiting on, or withdraws a\nquestion by its id. `relo listen` streams every answer this login receives over one connection, for\nservices that ask many questions. How questions behave: [Questions](/docs/concepts/questions); from\ncode: [Questions from code](/docs/guides/asking).\n\nBranch on the exit status, never on the wording: 0 means answered (read `state`; only `approved` is\npermission), 5 denied or no, 4 still open, 8 closed without an answer. The full table:\n[Exit codes](/docs/reference/exit-codes).\n\n```sh\nrelo ask \"Deploy 2.4 to production?\" --approval --detail \"Migration 0042 rewrites orders. Undo: rollback 0042.\"\n```\n\n## Commands\n\n### relo ask\n\n```sh\nrelo ask QUESTION [--dry-run] [--type approval|yes-no|choice] [--approval] [--yes-no]\n    [--option LABEL] [--detail TEXT] [--notification-only] [--expires-in DURATION]\n    [--timeout DURATION] [--no-wait] [--primary-label TEXT] [--secondary-label TEXT]\n    [--device ID] [--idempotency-key KEY] [--stdin] [--name NAME] [--source NAME]\n    [--project NAME] [--topic NAME] [--thread-name NAME] [--task-title TEXT]\n    [--computer NAME] [--account NAME] [--correlation-id ID] [--callback-url URL]\n    [--callback-token-file PATH]\n```\n\nAsk on this work's card and wait for the answer (inside a session, up to 100s). It never starts a card: with none running the question goes out as a notification with the answer buttons. The question is one line of at most 120 characters; the why and the risk go in --detail. Exit 0 approved/yes/chosen, 5 denied/no, 4 still open: run `relo interaction wait ID`, 8 closed without an answer (expired, canceled): do not act.\n\n| Option | What it does |\n| --- | --- |\n| `--dry-run` | Check everything locally (identity, limits, the plan) and print {ok,dryRun,would:{command,body}}: no request, no login needed. |\n| `--type approval|yes-no|choice` | Answer type (choice is implied by --option). |\n| `--approval` | Approve/Deny buttons. |\n| `--yes-no` | Yes/No buttons. |\n| `--option LABEL` | One answer of a choice question (repeat 2-4 times). LABEL, or ID=LABEL to choose the id; labels are one line of up to 24 characters. The reply reports state \"chosen\" with option and label. |\n| `--detail TEXT` | The question's explanation (why, risk, what changes), markdown up to 4,000 characters, read in Relo. |\n| `--notification-only` | Send the question as a notification with its answer buttons and never take a Live Activity card (for apps that should not crowd the Lock Screen). |\n| `--expires-in DURATION` | How long the question stays answerable: default 5m, up to the server's limit (7 days unless the admin changed it). Past 8h the card ends and the question keeps waiting in Relo. |\n| `--timeout DURATION` | How long to wait here for the answer. Default: the shorter of --expires-in and 300s (100s inside a session, whose shell tool kills long commands); at most --expires-in. Any length works: the wait runs in slices of 90s. The question stays answerable until it expires: resume with `relo interaction wait ID`. |\n| `--no-wait` | Return as soon as the question is on the card instead of waiting for the answer. |\n| `--primary-label TEXT` | Primary button label on a Live Activity question. |\n| `--secondary-label TEXT` | Secondary button label on a Live Activity question. |\n| `--device ID` | Target one phone by ID (repeatable). Omit to reach every phone. |\n| `--idempotency-key KEY` | Retry-safe key: a replay returns the first result without a second push. |\n| `--stdin` | Read a JSON object from stdin; flags win over its fields. |\n| `--name NAME` | Pin an explicit card name instead of the session or topic. |\n| `--source NAME` | Sender name shown on the phone, e.g. Claude Code or Release bot. Auto-detected for Claude Code, Codex, OpenCode, Gemini CLI and Cursor; any other harness sets RELO_SOURCE=\"<harness>\". |\n| `--project NAME` | Project the message is filed under. Defaults to the git repository name. |\n| `--topic NAME` | Thread within the project, e.g. a task or PR name. Messages with the same topic group together. |\n| `--thread-name NAME` | Alias for --topic. |\n| `--task-title TEXT` | Short title for the current task. |\n| `--computer NAME` | Computer name shown on the card. Automatic: RELO_COMPUTER, else the Mac's name, else the hostname. |\n| `--account NAME` | Agent account shown on the card (e.g. work, personal). Automatic: RELO_ACCOUNT, else `relo account NAME` (any harness), else the name of a custom config folder ($CLAUDE_CONFIG_DIR, $CODEX_HOME). |\n| `--correlation-id ID` | Your own ID, echoed back on the answer callback. |\n| `--callback-url URL` | Public https:// endpoint that receives the answer as a signed POST (retried 10 times over about 72 hours). |\n| `--callback-token-file PATH` | File holding the bearer token sent with the callback (16-512 characters). |\n\n### relo interaction get\n\n```sh\nrelo interaction get ID\n```\n\nRead a question's state and answer.\n\n### relo interaction wait\n\n```sh\nrelo interaction wait ID [--timeout DURATION]\n```\n\nResume waiting for an answer (default 60s; 100s inside a session).\n\n| Option | What it does |\n| --- | --- |\n| `--timeout DURATION` | How long to wait for the answer (default 60s; 100s inside a session; at most 1h). Any length works: the wait runs in slices of 90s. Exit 4 means still open: run it again. |\n\n### relo interaction cancel\n\n```sh\nrelo interaction cancel ID\n```\n\nWithdraw a pending question.\n\n### relo listen\n\n```sh\nrelo listen [--since CURSOR|TIME] [--once] [--timeout DURATION]\n```\n\nStream every answer to the questions this login asked, one JSON line each ({id,eventId,state,action,option?,label?,correlationId?,respondedAt,cursor}), over one long-lived connection the app opens. Ends with {cursor,received}. Resume after a restart with --since CURSOR.\n\nThe owner's command: refused inside an agent session.\n\n| Option | What it does |\n| --- | --- |\n| `--since CURSOR|TIME` | Resume after this cursor (from an earlier line) or start at this ISO time. Without it, only new answers. |\n| `--once` | One round (up to 60s), then exit. |\n| `--timeout DURATION` | Stop after this long (otherwise it listens until stopped). |\n",
