   "markdown": "# relo notify\n\nEvery option of the one-shot message about a finished outcome.\n\n`relo notify` sends one notification. Use it sparingly: a work's finish outcome already is the\nnotification, so `relo notify` is for a result that has no open work, such as a backup that ran\nwithout a card. It never asks: a question is `relo ask`. `relo notify withdraw` removes a delivered\nnotification from the phone. When notifications alert and when they stay quiet:\n[Notifications](/docs/concepts/notifications).\n\n```sh\nrelo notify \"Nightly backup finished: 42 GB in 18 minutes\" --title \"nightly-backup\"\n```\n\n## Commands\n\n### relo notify\n\n```sh\nrelo notify BODY... [--dry-run] [--title TEXT] [--summary TEXT] [--format text|markdown]\n    [--markdown] [--image URL] [--url URL] [--device ID] [--idempotency-key KEY]\n    [--source NAME] [--project NAME] [--topic NAME] [--thread-name NAME]\n    [--task-title TEXT] [--computer NAME] [--account NAME] [--stdin]\n```\n\nSparingly: a one-shot message about a finished outcome. Never a question. Inside a session the topic comes from the session's card.\n\nAlso: `relo notify send`.\n\n| Option | What it does |\n| --- | --- |\n| `--dry-run` | Check everything locally (identity, limits, the plan) and print {ok,dryRun,would:{command,body}}: no request, no login needed. |\n| `--title TEXT` | Message or activity title. Longer text is shortened at a word boundary with an ellipsis, and the reply carries a note. |\n| `--summary TEXT` | Short banner text for a long body; the full body stays readable in the app. Longer text is shortened, with a note. |\n| `--format text|markdown` | How the body is rendered in the app. |\n| `--markdown` | Shorthand for --format markdown. |\n| `--image URL` | Public https:// image shown with the message and as the sender avatar. |\n| `--url URL` | Opened from the message: https:// link, an app link (your-app://path), or shortcuts://run-shortcut?name=... |\n| `--device ID` | Target one phone by ID (repeatable). Omit to reach every phone. |\n| `--idempotency-key KEY` | Retry-safe key: a replay returns the first result without a second push. |\n| `--source NAME` | Sender name shown on the phone, e.g. Claude Code or Release bot. Auto-detected for Claude Code, Codex, OpenCode, Gemini CLI and Cursor; any other harness sets RELO_SOURCE=\"<harness>\". |\n| `--project NAME` | Project the message is filed under. Defaults to the git repository name. |\n| `--topic NAME` | Thread within the project, e.g. a task or PR name. Messages with the same topic group together. |\n| `--thread-name NAME` | Alias for --topic. |\n| `--task-title TEXT` | Short title for the current task. |\n| `--computer NAME` | Computer name shown on the card. Automatic: RELO_COMPUTER, else the Mac's name, else the hostname. |\n| `--account NAME` | Agent account shown on the card (e.g. work, personal). Automatic: RELO_ACCOUNT, else `relo account NAME` (any harness), else the name of a custom config folder ($CLAUDE_CONFIG_DIR, $CODEX_HOME). |\n| `--stdin` | Read a JSON object from stdin; flags win over its fields. |\n\n### relo notify withdraw\n\n```sh\nrelo notify withdraw ID [--idempotency-key KEY]\n```\n\nRemove a delivered notification from the phone.\n\n| Option | What it does |\n| --- | --- |\n| `--idempotency-key KEY` | Retry-safe key: a replay returns the first result without a second push. |\n",
