   "markdown": "# relo admin, relo sessions and relo activity\n\nThe owner's views and fixes across every session: open works, sessions and cards.\n\nEverything else in Relo is scoped to the session or producer that owns it: an agent sees only its own\nwork. `relo admin` is the deliberate exception. It acts as your terminal does, across every session of\nthe account, so you can see what each one shows and end work that hangs.\n\n- `relo admin works` lists every open and paused work, with its session and last update.\n- `relo admin finish` ends a work that hangs: one that is paused, or quiet for 20 minutes. A work that\n  is still moving stays its own session's and answers `work_running`.\n- `relo sessions` lists the sessions the server knows from hooks (empty without them). `relo activity`\n  reads, explains and ends cards.\n\nAn agent runs these only when you ask it for help, for example to clear a hanging or test card or to\ncheck what every session shows. It never uses them to change another session's work on its own.\n\n```sh\nrelo admin works\nrelo admin finish wrk_8f2c --dropped --outcome \"Test card from a setup check\"\n```\n\n## Commands\n\n### relo activity end\n\n```sh\nrelo activity end [CARD] [--dry-run] [--name NAME] [--status TEXT] [--detail TEXT]\n    [--clear-detail] [--progress n/m] [--clear-progress]\n    [--symbol terminal|code|build|success|warning] [--accent-color TEXT]\n    [--dismiss-after DURATION] [--if-sequence N] [--idempotency-key KEY] [--stdin]\n```\n\nFinish this work's card. Without --status it reads 'Complete' with a success icon.\n\nAcross every session, as the owner: `relo admin activity end`.\n\n| Option | What it does |\n| --- | --- |\n| `--dry-run` | Check everything locally (identity, limits, the plan) and print {ok,dryRun,would:{command,body}}: no request, no login needed. |\n| `--name NAME` | Pin an explicit card name instead of the session or topic. |\n| `--status TEXT` | What is happening now, in one short line. Work refuses text over 120 characters; a card shortens longer text and says so in a note. |\n| `--detail TEXT` | The question's explanation (why, risk, what changes), markdown up to 4,000 characters, read in Relo. |\n| `--clear-detail` | Remove the detail line. |\n| `--progress n/m` | A percent (40%), a fraction 0 to 1 or a count done/total (3/10). Never a guess from time; a bare number above 1 is rejected as ambiguous. |\n| `--clear-progress` | Remove progress. |\n| `--symbol terminal|code|build|success|warning` | Activity icon. |\n| `--accent-color TEXT` | Accent color. |\n| `--dismiss-after DURATION` | How long the finished card lingers (0 to 4h). |\n| `--if-sequence N` | Apply only if the activity is still at this sequence. |\n| `--idempotency-key KEY` | Retry-safe key: a replay returns the first result without a second push. |\n| `--stdin` | Read a JSON object from stdin; flags win over its fields. |\n\n### relo activity status\n\n```sh\nrelo activity status [CARD] [--name NAME] [--source NAME] [--project NAME]\n    [--topic NAME] [--thread-name NAME] [--stdin]\n```\n\nThis work's card, if one is running.\n\nThe owner's command: refused inside an agent session; `relo admin activity status` runs it across sessions.\n\n| Option | What it does |\n| --- | --- |\n| `--name NAME` | Pin an explicit card name instead of the session or topic. |\n| `--source NAME` | Sender name shown on the phone, e.g. Claude Code or Release bot. Auto-detected for Claude Code, Codex, OpenCode, Gemini CLI and Cursor; any other harness sets RELO_SOURCE=\"<harness>\". |\n| `--project NAME` | Project the message is filed under. Defaults to the git repository name. |\n| `--topic NAME` | Thread within the project, e.g. a task or PR name. Messages with the same topic group together. |\n| `--thread-name NAME` | Alias for --topic. |\n| `--stdin` | Read a JSON object from stdin; flags win over its fields. |\n\n### relo activity diagnose\n\n```sh\nrelo activity diagnose [CARD] [--name NAME] [--wait] [--timeout DURATION]\n```\n\nExplain why a card is or is not on the phone.\n\nThe owner's command: refused inside an agent session; `relo admin activity diagnose` runs it across sessions.\n\n| Option | What it does |\n| --- | --- |\n| `--name NAME` | Pin an explicit card name instead of the session or topic. |\n| `--wait` | Wait for the phone to report the card. |\n| `--timeout DURATION` | How long --wait waits (default 30s). |\n\n### relo activity get\n\n```sh\nrelo activity get [CARD] [--name NAME] [--source NAME] [--project NAME] [--topic NAME]\n    [--thread-name NAME] [--stdin]\n```\n\nRead a card by ID or name (even an ended one); with no CARD, the same as status.\n\nThe owner's command: refused inside an agent session; `relo admin activity get` runs it across sessions.\n\n| Option | What it does |\n| --- | --- |\n| `--name NAME` | Pin an explicit card name instead of the session or topic. |\n| `--source NAME` | Sender name shown on the phone, e.g. Claude Code or Release bot. Auto-detected for Claude Code, Codex, OpenCode, Gemini CLI and Cursor; any other harness sets RELO_SOURCE=\"<harness>\". |\n| `--project NAME` | Project the message is filed under. Defaults to the git repository name. |\n| `--topic NAME` | Thread within the project, e.g. a task or PR name. Messages with the same topic group together. |\n| `--thread-name NAME` | Alias for --topic. |\n| `--stdin` | Read a JSON object from stdin; flags win over its fields. |\n\n### relo activity list\n\n```sh\nrelo activity list [--limit 1..100]\n```\n\nList recent cards, newest first: id, state, title, status, step, progress, updatedAt. --full for everything.\n\nThe owner's command: refused inside an agent session; `relo admin activity list` runs it across sessions.\n\n| Option | What it does |\n| --- | --- |\n| `--limit 1..100` | How many cards to list (1 to 100, default 10). |\n\n### relo sessions\n\n```sh\nrelo sessions [--live]\n```\n\nSessions the server knows from optional hooks (empty without them): harness, computer, account, project, phase (working|waiting|idle|ended), waitingFor (input|turn, when waiting), lastSeenAt, card; plus counts by phase. --live: only working and waiting.\n\nThe owner's command: refused inside an agent session; `relo admin sessions` runs it across sessions.\n\n| Option | What it does |\n| --- | --- |\n| `--live` | Only the sessions working now or waiting for the owner; the counts still cover every phase. |\n\n### relo admin works\n\n```sh\nrelo admin works [--all]\n```\n\nOwner administration (only when the owner asks; normal work stays in its own session): every open and paused work of the account with its session, state and last update; --all includes finished ones.\n\n| Option | What it does |\n| --- | --- |\n| `--all` | Every work of the account, finished ones too, not only open and paused. |\n\n### relo admin finish\n\n```sh\nrelo admin finish WORK [--outcome TEXT] [--dropped] [--failed]\n```\n\nOwner administration: end a hanging work of any session (paused, or quiet 20 minutes; a moving work answers work_running) with an outcome; --dropped or --failed when it did not succeed.\n\n| Option | What it does |\n| --- | --- |\n| `--outcome TEXT` | What happened, in the owner's words. Required; it is the notification. |\n| `--dropped` | The work was abandoned (History only). |\n| `--failed` | The work did not succeed (the owner gets an alert). |\n",
