   "markdown": "# Machine and advanced commands\n\nThe commands harnesses launch, the machine-readable reference, and the advanced delivery, evidence and outbox tools.\n\nNobody types most of these. A harness launches `relo mcp` (a stdio MCP server for tools without a\nshell) and `relo hook` (the optional hook entry point that `relo setup --level guide` installs). `relo help`\nand `relo schema` are the reference in the terminal: `relo help COMMAND` for one command, `relo help\nall` for everything, `relo schema` for the same as JSON.\n\nThe rest are advanced and for troubleshooting. `relo delivery reconcile` settles a push whose fate is\nunknown, `relo evidence timeline` and `relo evidence metrics` show delivery evidence, and `relo outbox\nstatus` and `relo outbox flush` show and send the changes this computer still has queued (offline\nwrites and session snapshots). See [Troubleshooting](/docs/troubleshooting).\n\n## Commands\n\n### relo delivery reconcile\n\n```sh\nrelo delivery reconcile JOB_ID mark-accepted|retry|cancel\n```\n\nOperator recovery for an ambiguous push.\n\n### relo evidence timeline\n\n```sh\nrelo evidence timeline [--notification ID] [--limit 1..100] [--cursor CURSOR]\n```\n\nDelivery evidence for debugging.\n\n| Option | What it does |\n| --- | --- |\n| `--notification ID` | Notification ID filter. |\n| `--limit 1..100` | How many items to return (1 to 100). |\n| `--cursor CURSOR` | Pagination cursor from a previous page. |\n\n### relo evidence metrics\n\n```sh\nrelo evidence metrics\n```\n\nDelivery metrics for debugging.\n\n### relo outbox status\n\n```sh\nrelo outbox status\n```\n\nWhat is queued locally for the server (offline writes, session snapshots): {pending:{observed,declared,total},oldestAt?,dead:[{at,lane,route,status,reason}],harnessCredential:present|missing}. Read-only.\n\n### relo outbox flush\n\n```sh\nrelo outbox flush\n```\n\nSend what is queued, oldest first (a hook that queued a snapshot starts it in the background; one flusher at a time; it first resolves and checks the liveness of session processes, and deletes local state of sessions ended over 8 days ago). Prints {sent,pending,dead,locked?}.\n\n### relo hook\n\n```sh\nrelo hook EVENT [--agent NAME]\n```\n\nHook entry point (optional; only `relo setup --level guide` installs it, never typed; cards, questions and notifications work identically without it): reads the harness hook JSON on stdin, updates this session's local phase (open|working|waiting|stopped|ended) and queues a snapshot only when the phase changes (plus a heartbeat at most every 5 minutes while working): the session id hash, phase and its times, open-tool time, project, computer and account, sent in the background with this computer's harness credential. Never prompts, tool names or tool input/output. Prints nothing and always exits 0. EVENT: start|prompt|tool-start|tool-end|wait|stop|end|subagent-start|subagent-stop|compact (subagents roll up into their session), or a local role: remind|restore|turn.\n\n| Option | What it does |\n| --- | --- |\n| `--agent NAME` | The harness sending the event (set by the installed hook entry). |\n\n### relo mcp\n\n```sh\nrelo mcp\n```\n\nA stdio MCP server for harnesses without a shell (Claude desktop, Cursor chat, Codex, Gemini CLI; VS Code reads it from a project's .vscode/mcp.json, which Relo does not write); a harness launches it, nobody types it. Tools: relo_work_start, relo_work_update, relo_work_finish, relo_work_state, relo_ask (waits up to 5 minutes with progress notifications), relo_interaction_wait, relo_notify, relo_doctor; results are the same compact JSON. Each connection is one session. The owner adds it with `relo setup --mcp --agent NAME`.\n\n### relo help\n\n```sh\nrelo help [identity|all]\n```\n\nShort guide; `help identity` or `help all` for more.\n\n### relo schema\n\n```sh\nrelo schema [COMMAND...]\n```\n\nThis machine-readable reference; `relo schema work update` (or work.update) prints only those commands plus exitCodes.\n",
